hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19244","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi from his father from his uncle Fulan ibn Umaylah from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are four, and deeds are six. People: one with plenty in this world and the Hereafter, one with plenty in this world and straitened in the Hereafter, one straitened in this world with plenty in the Hereafter, and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. Deeds: two obligating, like for like, tenfold, and seven hundred fold. The two obligating: whoever dies Muslim believing, associating nothing with Allah, Paradise is assured for him; whoever dies disbelieving, the Fire is assured for him. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, Allah knowing that his heart has felt it and was keen on it, one good is written for him. Whoever intends an evil deed it is not written against him; whoever does it, one is written and not multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed it is ten like it for him. Whoever spends an expense in the path of Allah it is seven hundred fold for him."
"19245","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari narrated to us from his father from Yusayr ibn Umaylah from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever spends an expense in the path of Allah, it is written seven hundred fold."
"19246","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr meaning Ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Shamir ibn Atiyyah from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What a good man you are, O Khuraym, were it not for two traits. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your trailing your lower garment, and your letting down your hair."
"19247","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us from Zaidah from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari from his father from Yusayr ibn Umaylah from Khuraym ibn Fatik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends an expense in the path of Allah, it is multiplied seven hundred fold."
"19248","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi from his father from Khuraym ibn Fatik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are six, and people are four. Two obligating, like for like, the good deed tenfold, and the good deed seven hundred. As for the two obligating: whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah enters the Fire. As for like for like: whoever intends a good deed until his heart feels it, Allah knowing that of him, one good is written for him. Whoever does an evil deed, one evil is written against him. Whoever does a good deed, ten like it are written for him. Whoever spends an expense in the path of Allah, a good deed is seven hundred. People are four: with plenty in this world and straitened in the Hereafter, with plenty in the Hereafter and straitened in this world, with plenty in this world and the Hereafter, and straitened in this world and the Hereafter."
